<?xml version="1.0"?>
<ScenContainer xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xmlns:xsd="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema">
  <ScenTitle>Battles of the 3rd WW, Tattletale, 1991</ScenTitle>
  <ScenDescription>&lt;BODY scroll=auto&gt;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style="MARGIN: 0cm 0cm 8pt"&gt;&lt;SPAN style="mso-ansi-language: EN-CA"&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;This scenario is loosely based on Larry Bond’s ‘Battles of the Third World War’ for the Harpoon board game. © 1987 by Game Designers’ Workshop, Inc.&lt;?xml:namespace prefix = "o" ns = "urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:office" /&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P class=MsoNormal style="MARGIN: 0cm 0cm 8pt"&gt;&lt;B style="mso-bidi-font-weight: normal"&gt;&lt;SPAN style="mso-ansi-language: EN-CA"&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;Tattletale &lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/B&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P class=MsoNormal style="MARGIN: 0cm 0cm 8pt"&gt;&lt;B style="mso-bidi-font-weight: normal"&gt;&lt;SPAN style="mso-ansi-language: EN-CA"&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;15 May 1991&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/B&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P class=MsoNormal style="MARGIN: 0cm 0cm 8pt"&gt;&lt;SPAN style="mso-ansi-language: EN-CA"&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;STANAVFORLANT is NATO’s Standing Naval Force Atlantic, composition of STANAVFORLANT is constantly changing but is currently made up of five combat ships and an Oiler. The force is tasked conducting ASW operations in the Norwegian Sea and is being shadowed by a Soviet Mod Kashin class guided missile destroyer. Tensions are high but the world is still at peace.&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P class=MsoNormal style="MARGIN: 0cm 0cm 8pt"&gt;&lt;SPAN style="mso-ansi-language: EN-CA"&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P class=MsoNormal style="MARGIN: 0cm 0cm 8pt"&gt;&lt;SPAN style="mso-ansi-language: EN-CA"&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;Designers notes:&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P class=MsoListParagraphCxSpFirst style="MARGIN: 0cm 0cm 0pt 36pt; TEXT-INDENT: -18pt; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1"&gt;&lt;SPAN style="FONT-FAMILY: Symbol; mso-ansi-language: EN-CA; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-family: Symbol"&gt;&lt;SPAN style="mso-list: Ignore"&gt;·&lt;SPAN style='FONT: 7pt "Times New Roman"'&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style="mso-ansi-language: EN-CA"&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;Playable by either side. Blue = NATO, Red = Soviet.&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P class=MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle style="MARGIN: 0cm 0cm 0pt 36pt; TEXT-INDENT: -18pt; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1"&gt;&lt;SPAN style="FONT-FAMILY: Symbol; mso-ansi-language: EN-CA; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-family: Symbol"&gt;&lt;SPAN style="mso-list: Ignore"&gt;·&lt;SPAN style='FONT: 7pt "Times New Roman"'&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style="mso-ansi-language: EN-CA"&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;The Soviet ship will start randomly either very close to the NATO ships or beyond visual range near the max range of the SS-N-2c missiles. Any other position seems almost suicidal for no gain.&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P class=MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle style="MARGIN: 0cm 0cm 0pt 36pt; TEXT-INDENT: -18pt; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1"&gt;&lt;SPAN style="FONT-FAMILY: Symbol; mso-ansi-language: EN-CA; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-family: Symbol"&gt;&lt;SPAN style="mso-list: Ignore"&gt;·&lt;SPAN style='FONT: 7pt "Times New Roman"'&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style="mso-ansi-language: EN-CA"&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;At a random time very early in the scenario Blue will become hostile to Red. If Red is the player you have a few minutes before you become a target to Blue, which also happens at a random time but a few minutes later.&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P class=MsoListParagraphCxSpLast style="MARGIN: 0cm 0cm 8pt 36pt; TEXT-INDENT: -18pt; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1"&gt;&lt;SPAN style="FONT-FAMILY: Symbol; mso-ansi-language: EN-CA; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-family: Symbol"&gt;&lt;SPAN style="mso-list: Ignore"&gt;·&lt;SPAN style='FONT: 7pt "Times New Roman"'&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style="mso-ansi-language: EN-CA"&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;Scoring does not match the original scenario setup exactly.&lt;SPAN style="mso-spacerun: yes"&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/SPAN&gt;The Soviet player should sink at least three ships to gain a total victory. The NATO side should preserve its force and sink the Soviet ship once hostilities start.&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P class=MsoListParagraphCxSpLast style="MARGIN: 0cm 0cm 8pt 36pt; TEXT-INDENT: -18pt; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1"&gt;&lt;SPAN style="mso-ansi-language: EN-CA"&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&lt;SPAN style="mso-ansi-language: EN-CA"&gt;
&lt;P class=MsoNormal style="MARGIN: 0cm 0cm 8pt"&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;&lt;B style="mso-bidi-font-weight: normal"&gt;&lt;I style="mso-bidi-font-style: normal"&gt;&lt;SPAN style="mso-ansi-language: EN-CA"&gt;Note&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/I&gt;&lt;/B&gt;&lt;I style="mso-bidi-font-style: normal"&gt;&lt;SPAN style="mso-ansi-language: EN-CA"&gt;: this is quite simple to play as the NATO player and quite challenging as the WP. So if you’re just starting out, choosing Blue will give you a relatively easy win but you can experiment with weapons allocation and a few other bits.&lt;SPAN style="mso-spacerun: yes"&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/SPAN&gt;A more advanced player should try a hand as the Red player.&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/I&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/BODY&gt;</ScenDescription>
  <Complexity>1</Complexity>
  <Difficulty>1</Difficulty>
  <ScenSetting>Norwegean Sea</ScenSetting>
  <ScenDate>1991</ScenDate>
  <DBVersion>DB3K_491.db3</DBVersion>
  <Scenario_Compressed></Scenario_Compressed>
